Files taken from gpu-lexer (generated by scripts/sync-upstream.mjs, unmodified
unless noted):

  model/weights-int6-active.bin   packages/training/active/weights-int6-active.bin
                                  (promoted checkpoint 20261117T071411.182Z)
  model/model-active.json         packages/training/active/model-active.json
  model/runtime-weights.txt       WEIGHTS of packages/core/src/model.runtime.generated.js
  model/shader-f16.wgsl,          createPromotedShader() of
  model/shader-f32.wgsl           packages/core/src/shader.min.generated.js,
                                  MODIFIED: the in-block top-down pass of
                                  tree_down_classify computes a level's children
                                  before writing them (a workgroup-memory race fix)
  js/gpu-lexer.js                 dist/index.js of gpu-lexer@0.0.6 (npm), with the
                                  same shader fix and a bridge appended
  src/generated/*.rs              constants generated from the files above

The Rust code in src/prepare.rs, src/cpu.rs, src/spans.rs and src/gpu.rs ports
upstream's packages/core/src/prepare-tree.js, tree-features.js, spans.js, gpu.js
and packages/training/src/tree-model.js.

The model weights are distributed by upstream under the MIT License above (in
the repository and in the npm package). Per upstream's MODEL_CARD.md, the model
was trained on permissively licensed, pinned repositories and npm packages
(packages/training/data/corpus.json upstream) with labels from Shiki 4.4.3 (MIT);
no training source is redistributed here. See upstream's MODEL_CARD.md for the
model's intended use and limitations, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the tools
used to build it.

The test fixtures in fixtures/src are third-party source files under their own
licenses; fixtures/sources.json lists each file's origin and license.

The TextView/Editor color palette in src/nsh/text_view.rs and tsx/tokens.ts
repeats the colors of nsh-base's built-in highlighting (Apache-2.0) so that
gpu-lexer's tokens look like the built-in ones.
